{"seq":13,"trial_id":"matrix-mu-2026-11/qm-pi-opus-none-mu-v03-dev/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r4","wall_ts":"2026-11-05T07:58:26.711Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"cd5f192a3d62e9a3ad2f2a2746e398745ba1e2af25095945687490962e741bb4","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DMATRIX0001","text":"I found two ticket numbers for Quarrendon Freight Lines in Moss's notes:\n\n1. **#PD-4492**, from *\"Moss: Sunday prep for Ruth\"* (teams/team-north/digests/2025-10-05-north-sunday.md). Thea Ramaswell opened it on 4 Oct 2025 because drivers on the 04:00 shift at Dock Doors 14–18 in the Eau Claire yard weren't getting SMS bay assignments at the gatehouse kiosk. Support patched it that evening, and Thea confirmed it was fixed on 5 Oct. The note also has an action item to archive the Eau Claire kiosk logs before the 14 Oct maintenance window.\n2. **#4419**, from *\"Moss: North cheat sheet (undated)\"* (teams/team-north/digests/north-account-cheatsheet.md). Thea logged it because the gatehouse barcode scanners couldn't read trailer tags at Door 14 during third shift. It was escalated to tier-2 product support for scanner firmware testing.\n\nWhere I found nothing:\n- Moss's other North notes mention QFL but have no ticket numbers. The 9/14 pipeline digest covers Thea's question about appointment time vs. gate arrival, and the 3/23 renewal check-in covers the renewal.\n- #4409, #4412 and FR-882 are in Moss's Central notes, but they belong to Marrow accounts, not QFL.\n- Marcus has a note on \"Quarendon Freightways,\" spelled with one \"r.\" That's a different company and not one of our customers, so I left it out."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DMATRIX0001","ts":"1791987000.000124"}}
